---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const canonical = new URL('/privacy-policy/', Astro.site).href;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — RealWordCounter"
  description="RealWordCounter's privacy policy. Learn how we handle your data — spoiler: we don't collect any. All text processing happens 100% in your browser."
  canonical={canonical}
  ogImage="og-home.png"
>

  <div class="container" style="padding-top:var(--space-8);padding-bottom:var(--space-4)">
    <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a>
      <span class="breadcrumb-sep">›</span>
      <span class="breadcrumb-current">Privacy Policy</span>
    </nav>
  </div>

  <div class="container policy-wrap">
    <div class="policy-header">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="policy-meta">Last updated: June 2025 · Effective immediately</p>
      <p class="policy-intro">
        RealWordCounter is built on a simple principle: <strong>your text is yours</strong>.
        We do not collect it, store it, or process it on any server. This page explains
        exactly what we do — and don't — do with any information related to your use of this site.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="policy-body">

      <section class="policy-section">
        <h2>1. No Text Is Ever Collected</h2>
        <p>
          Every feature on RealWordCounter — word count, character count, readability analysis,
          keyword density, platform limits checker, UPSC presets — runs entirely in your browser
          using JavaScript. Your text is <strong>never sent to our servers</strong>. We have no
          server-side processing of any content you type or paste into our tools.
        </p>
        <p>
          The only place your draft is stored is your own browser's <code>localStorage</code>,
          which is accessible only by you on your device. Clearing your browser data removes it.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="policy-section">
        <h2>2. What We Do Collect</h2>
        <p>We collect minimal, anonymised data to understand how the site is used:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Page views and navigation paths</strong> — via Google Analytics (anonymised IP). This tells us which tools are most used, nothing about content.</li>
          <li><strong>Device and browser type</strong> — to ensure compatibility and fix rendering issues.</li>
          <li><strong>Country and region</strong> — to confirm we are serving our primary audience (India) correctly.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We do <strong>not</strong> collect: your name, email address, text content, uploaded files,
          IP address (full), or any personally identifiable information unless you voluntarily submit
          our contact form.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="policy-section">
        <h2>3. Contact Form Data</h2>
        <p>
          If you send us a message via the <a href="/contact">Contact page</a>, your name, email
          address, and message are processed by
          <a href="https://web3forms.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Web3Forms</a>
          and delivered to our inbox. We use this data only to respond to your enquiry.
          We do not add you to any mailing list or share your details with third parties.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="policy-section">
        <h2>4. Cookies</h2>
        <p>
          We use only one first-party cookie: a <strong>theme preference</strong> stored in
          <code>localStorage</code> (light/dark mode). This is not a tracking cookie and contains
          no personal information.
        </p>
        <p>
          Google Analytics may set anonymised analytics cookies. You can opt out of Google Analytics
          by installing the
          <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Analytics opt-out browser add-on</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="policy-section">
        <h2>5. Third-Party Services</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Google Analytics</strong> — anonymised usage statistics</li>
          <li><strong>Google Fonts</strong> — the Inter typeface is loaded from Google's CDN</li>
          <li><strong>Web3Forms</strong> — contact form submission processing</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Each of these services has its own privacy policy. We have no control over their data
          practices and encourage you to review their policies directly.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="policy-section">
        <h2>6. Children's Privacy</h2>
        <p>
          RealWordCounter does not knowingly collect any information from children under the age
          of 13. If you are a parent or guardian and believe your child has submitted personal data
          via our contact form, please contact us and we will delete it promptly.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="policy-section">
        <h2>7. Your Rights</h2>
        <p>
          Since we store no personal data beyond voluntarily submitted contact form messages,
          there is very little to request. However, you may:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Request deletion of any contact form message you submitted</li>
          <li>Clear your browser's localStorage at any time to remove your saved drafts</li>
          <li>Opt out of Google Analytics using the link in section 4</li>
        </ul>
        <p>To exercise these rights, email us via the <a href="/contact">Contact page</a>.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="policy-section">
        <h2>8. Changes to This Policy</h2>
        <p>
          We may update this privacy policy from time to time. The "Last updated" date at the top
          of this page reflects when it was last revised. Continued use of the site after changes
          are posted constitutes acceptance of the updated policy.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="policy-section">
        <h2>9. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about this policy? Reach us via the <a href="/contact">Contact page</a>.
          We aim to respond within 48 hours on weekdays.
        </p>
      </section>

    </div>
  </div>

</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .policy-wrap {
    max-width: 800px;
    padding-bottom: var(--space-16);
  }

  .policy-header {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-10);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-8);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-hairline);
  }

  .policy-header h1 {
    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 3vw, 2.5rem);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }

  .policy-meta {
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--color-mute);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .policy-intro {
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--color-body);
  }

  .policy-body {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-8);
  }

  .policy-section h2 {
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }

  .policy-section p {
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--color-body);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }

  .policy-section ul {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-3) var(--space-6);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-2);
  }

  .policy-section li {
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--color-body);
  }

  .policy-section code {
    background: var(--color-canvas-soft-2);
    padding: 1px 5px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 13px;
  }

  .policy-section a {
    color: var(--color-primary);
    font-weight: 500;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .policy-section a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
</style>
